<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolesław II the Bald</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1220–<a href="/years/1278">1278</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Bolesław II Rogatka</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolesław II the Bald was a Silesian Piast duke, eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-the-pious">Henry II the Pious</a>, who was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legnica">Legnica</a> in 1241. Quarrelsome and violent, he lost Silesia to divisions with his brothers and in 1248 kept the Duchy of Legnica. He invited German settlers and founded towns. After his death his lands were split among his sons, creating the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawor">Jawor</a>.</p></div>
